nalysis of  the Warren's speech match mine Trump  also seems to be adopting my  pronunciation of Pete Buddha jej  tweeting quote boot edge edge  parentheses Buddha  he's doing pretty well tonight giving  crazy Bernie a run for his money very  interesting I would be shocked if Trump  is actually getting that from me that  would definitely be something else so  let's talk delegate totals delegate  totals as of right now as I told you  insignificant in terms of the delegate  math you need 1990 delegates to secure  the nomination all that the current  numbers tell us is that we are starting  to see enough of a split in the delegate  math that if this trajectory continues  no one will get to 1990 and it will be a  contested convention we'll deal with  that in more detail tomorrow but looking  at totals Pete Budaj edge now with 22  delegates he has his 13 from Iowa plus 9  from last night  Bernie Sanders with 21 delegates he has  his 12 from Iowa plus 9 from last night  Warren has 8 Amy 7 and Joe Biden 6  nobody else has any delegates note that  for now Bernie Sanders has won the raw  votes in 100% of the primaries and  caucuses Iowa and New Hampshire but  Bernie Sanders is not willing winning  the delegate math and that is firing up  many many people  Andrew yang did drop out yesterday after  an abysmal 2.8 percent in New Hampshire  we're going to talk about that a little  later but now we go on to a presidential  debate next Wednesday that'll be  followed by voting in the Nevada  caucuses on Saturday February 22nd then  voting in South Carolina on Saturday  February 29th and then on to Super  Tuesday March 3rd which I believe will  really give us a sense of is the  trajectory continuing to look like a  contested convention are there really  two contenders right now it's Bernie and  Pete but you've got a bunch of people  that are still relatively close just a  few delegates separating everybody let's  look at those upcoming primaries and  caucuses we really don't know what the  hell is going on and you have in Nevada  because the last poll is a month old at  that point Biden was plus one over  Bernie that was a month ago  anything could happen in Nevada would  love to see some new polling there  south carolina has been widely expected  and assumed to go to joe biden for a  while now the latest poll is ten days  old and it has biden plus 18  I do believe South Carolina is  essentially a must-win for Biden now  realistically Biden will stay in at  least until Super Tuesday because  anything could happen on Super Tuesday  but Biden is not going to do well on  Super Tuesday unless he can gain  momentum by securing the win in South  Carolina that he has long been expected  to get if he doesn't get South Carolina  the Biden path starts to narrow even  more than it has already narrowed not to  mention that Elizabeth Warren has to  start picking up delegates she's polling  fourth in South Carolina I wouldn't be  surprised to see her end up with zero in  South Carolina remember that like with  most primaries there's this 15%  viability threshold in South Carolina if  you don't get 15% you get 0 delegates  right now Warren is polling eighth in  South Carolina not looking good so there  are now in reaction to yesterday's  Bernie win over Budaj edge there are all  sorts of hot takes about what does New  Hampshire mean for Bernie what does it  mean for the nomination and the reality  is that you can spin this almost any way  you want and a lot of people are so  let's go through now later we'll talk  about yang getting out and who else  should get out let's now talk about the  hot takes being floated around under the  guise of being enlightened think pieces
 

